{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["It is written regarding Shavuot: ״שעיר עזים לכפר עליכם״, and it is not written לחטאת — because of the honor of the Torah, which was given on that day. And this is what the liturgical poet established: דיום הבכורים חטאת לא נזכר / למען יהי דבר המלך למנוחה. Another explanation: because Israel were then free of all sin, as it is said in the midrash: from when they accepted upon themselves the yoke of Torah and the commandments, I account it upon them as though they had never sinned. And this is what the liturgical poet established: בזולת של שבועות / קבלו מלכותי ולא תאשמו."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:17.718290345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}